+// Inline uniform updates (OP_UPDATE_UB) in a range are copy-on-write: a new copy gets the change, later bindings read the new copy, and earlier draws still read the old copy. The update also goes directly into game memory, so the first copy of the next submission includes it. The GPU never reads or writes a registered range itself, so an update needs no GPU copy and does not break the render pass.
